alright i know this is gonna disappoint  a ton of you guys  but i'm almost certain that the new  larger imac coming later this year  is still gonna have a chin and i'm gonna  explain why in this video  using some common sense as well as some  hints and tidbits  that i've recently figured out so let's  get right into it now before we begin  i want to give you guys some good news  and mention that in my opinion  there's a 50 50 chance that the larger  imac  actually comes with black bezels but i'm  gonna get into that in just a minute  but for now let's talk about the chin  the first question we have to answer  is why apple gave the new 24-inch imac  the chin  in the first place a lot of people are  going to say that the only reason they  kept it was so they could fit  the entire computer behind the chin and  keep it as thin as possible  yes that is totally true but in my  personal opinion  that wasn't the number one reason i  believe that apple's number one  requirement for the imac redesign  was quite literally to keep the chin and  here's why  the 24 inch imac is basically a  reincarnation  of the classic imac g3 and we know that  because it had white bezels  a chin and essentially the same color  options on  everything from the mac itself to the  mouse and the keyboard  and if you think about it every single  imac that featured the built into the  display concept  starting with the imac g5 in 2004 came  with the chin  and then the 2007 imac which came with  the chin  and then the 2012 imac which came with  the chin  and the main reason why they did that is  because that chin has always been  totally unique to apple  and has become an iconic design aspect  of  the imac making it instantly  recognizable  compared to every other all-in-one pc  out there  and that's why the 24-inch imac still  has the chin  it's iconic and believe it or not it's  the chin  that sells it for apple wanna know how i  know that well  take a look at all of these all-in-one  pcs they basically all have at least  some sort of a chin  with branding on it because they want it  to look like the classic imac but i did  find  a couple of them without a chin so take  a guess  just by looking at it which brand this  one is from  if you guessed hp you're wrong it's from  lenovo  and how about this one who made this all  in one  if you guessed dell you're wrong it's hp  and what about this one  yeah you get the point and that's the  main reason why it makes sense for apple  to keep the chin  for the larger imac as well but don't  worry because the chin  is actually going to look quite a lot  slimmer than the one on the 24 inch imac  and let me prove it to you believe it or  not but there were actually three sizes  of the core 2 dual imac  with white bezels a 17 inch a 20 inch  and a 24 inch and if you look closely  the chin is exactly the same thickness  on each model  looking quite a bit slimmer on the  largest 24 inch  and then on the 2007 aluminum bezel  models the chin  was also the same thickness and the same  thing for the slimmer imac design  that everybody has right now both the  21.5 inch and  27 inch imacs have the same exact  chin thickness so here's the point that  i'm trying to make  the chin on the larger imac is actually  going to look pretty slim  because it's going to be the same exact  thickness as the one on the 24 inch  but the display will be scaled up to as  much as  30 inches so the chin will look pretty  slim  like in this image created by a mac  rumors forum user  and since i believe that it's gonna have  a chin it's extremely unlikely  that it'll get a large 32 inch display  because it'll simply be too big being  even bigger than the size of the pro  display xdr  now since apple is going to scale the  imac up to basically look like a larger  version of the 24 inch imac  they can get away with making the body  itself thicker  while maintaining the same balanced  ratio in terms of the dimensions  for example a 30 inch display is 25  larger than a 24 inch display so they  can  actually make the body up to 25 thicker  so instead of being 11.5 millimeters  thin  like on the 24 inch they can actually  make the larger imac  a couple of millimeters thicker without  impacting the dimensions too much  and if you really think about it the  current 27 inch imac  is already 15 thicker than the 21 and a  half inch  so i expect them to do the exact same  thing on the larger imac  especially if it's getting a 30 inch  display what this essentially means is  that apple will  actually be able to fit in a more  powerful m1x chip  along with all of the other components  behind  the chin just like they're already doing  with the 24  inch and if you think about it the chin  on the larger imac  is also going to be much longer allowing  for a  longer logic board with more space for  other cooling components and wherever  else they need  so yeah i'm actually pretty confident  that apple will still be able to fit  the entire computer in the chin of the  larger imac  even with more performance and if that  wasn't enough for you  here are a few more pieces of evidence  pointing to the larger imac  getting a chin the new 24 inch imac has  a variety of different colors  but one of them is missing apple's  signature space gray  the fact that apple left that color  option out basically means that they're  planning to introduce it  in a larger imac and if that imac did  not have a chin  and it was all display in black bezels  there wouldn't really be that big of a  point to the space gray color option  since you could only really see it from  the side or from the back  so it makes sense to keep the chin  around for that space gray color but as  far as the other color options i  honestly don't know if all of them will  make it  or if apple is gonna try to keep the  larger imac more subtle with more  neutral colors  but i actually think that there's a  chance that apple could be  keeping the bezels white if you think  about it apple's larger imacs have  always looked  fundamentally identical to the smaller  models  so giving it black bezels would be a bit  weird unless  they decide to call it the imac pro and  then that changes  everything i initially thought that  that's what apple is gonna do  but after the release of the 24 inch  imac that definitely changed my  perspective a little bit  and i actually think that there's a  chance that apple could be releasing  two more imac models but that's another  topic for another video  so if you're interested in seeing that  video definitely subscribe  down below so you don't miss out now as  far as the specs of this new imac  i think the display resolution will be  somewhere between 5.2 and 5.5 k  depending on if it's getting a 28 or 30  inch display and i don't think that it's  going to be getting many led tech  it's going to be sticking to the  standard lcd and as for the chipset the  absolute simplest way for apple to  manufacture  this larger imac is to give every model  the m1x chip just like they did with the  m1 on the 24 inch imac  but there's also a small chance that it  could have  a more expensive m1z upgrade option  but i'm not really sure about this just  yet now we also heard rumors of apple  working on a dedicated  graphics chip for a larger imac coming  in the second half of this year  so that will likely be an upgrade option  that you'll have to pay  extra for if it comes it'll definitely  come with up to 32 gigabytes of ram  or maybe even 64 but i'm not really sure  about that  and will probably have up to eight  terabytes of ssd storage  just like on the current 27 inch imac so  there you guys go  that's pretty much all of my thoughts on  the new larger imac coming later this  year  and if you totally disagree with my  point of view  go ahead and comment your thoughts down  below but if you enjoyed this video  click that circle above to subscribe for  more videos like this one  definitely check out one of those two  right there thanks for watching and  we'll see you in  the next video  [Music]

